WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:08.372
The car pulled over on a dirt road, and the billionaire opened the car door.

2
00:00:08.373 --> 00:00:13.284
"Follow me to the P.O.D.'s hiding spot," Lainie said.

3
00:00:13.285 --> 00:00:16.939
Ally trudged along behind her on a desert path.

4
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.616
"I wish I had some proof that Lainie is a Carparian," she thought.

5
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:24.763
But how could she prove something like that?

6
00:00:24.764 --> 00:00:29.847
"I'm so excited you're going to be flying with me," Lainie said.

7
00:00:29.848 --> 00:00:32.761
"I think you'll find we have a lot in common.

8
00:00:32.762 --> 00:00:40.113
We're both adventurous, and we have the same taste in jewelry."

9
00:00:40.114 --> 00:00:44.564
"Plus, we're probably both from space!" Ally thought.

10
00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:50.769
Suddenly she remembered something her mother had told her when she first gave Ally the meld medallion:

11
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:55.055
"Your meld medallion will enable you to take on other forms.

12
00:00:55.056 --> 00:01:00.604
But when other beings wear it, it will reveal their true form."

13
00:01:00.605 --> 00:01:08.267
"Hmm," Ally thought. "I wonder if I could get Lainie to try on my meld medallion."

14
00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:15.696
The problem was, the second Ally removed the meld medallion, she would return to her Astralian form.

15
00:01:15.697 --> 00:01:23.071
She couldn't let that happen. But as they walked along, Ally kept thinking about it.

16
00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:26.675
Finally, she got the perfect idea.

17
00:01:26.676 --> 00:01:36.356
"It's dangerous," she told herself, "but so is flying into space with a Carparian. It's worth a try."

18
00:01:36.357 --> 00:01:41.361
Lainie led Ally behind a large rock formation where her P.O.D. was hidden.

19
00:01:41.362 --> 00:01:46.133
When Ally first spotted the spaceship, she thought she was seeing things.

20
00:01:46.134 --> 00:01:48.299
It looked a lot like her escape pod.

21
00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:55.778
It was the same shape and size, and the hatch opened the same way.

22
00:01:55.779 --> 00:02:00.009
Even the inside looked similar!

23
00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:05.795
But as soon as Lainie began the tour, Ally realized how different it was from her pod.

24
00:02:05.796 --> 00:02:14.375
"My P.O.D. is designed to go from zero to the speed of light in less than one minute," Lainie said.

25
00:02:14.376 --> 00:02:23.464
"It's designed with antilaser shields and galactic ray shades, and it has three onboard gamma cannons."

26
00:02:23.465 --> 00:02:29.270
Ally wiped her brow. "I remember learning about gamma cannons in school," she thought.

27
00:02:29.271 --> 00:02:33.325
"I think Carparians invented them."

28
00:02:33.326 --> 00:02:36.873
Ally closed her eyes for a second to gather all her courage.

29
00:02:36.874 --> 00:02:41.973
It was time to find out Lainie's true identity once and for all.

30
00:02:41.974 --> 00:02:47.288
As Lainie continued the tour, Ally casually began playing with the chain of her medallion.

31
00:02:47.289 --> 00:02:54.002
"The bathroom is through that door," Lainie said, "and all our food is stored in this cabinet.

32
00:02:54.003 --> 00:03:01.790
Everything is dehydrated and needs to . . ." She had just noticed Ally's meld medallion.

33
00:03:01.791 --> 00:03:09.145
"Remind me, Ally, where on earth did your parents get that amazing necklace?"

34
00:03:09.146 --> 00:03:14.530
"I'm not sure," Ally replied. "Would you like to see it up close?"

35
00:03:14.531 --> 00:03:18.692
Lainie's eyes lit up. "I'd love to!"

36
00:03:18.693 --> 00:03:24.877
Ally started to take the medallion off, but then she stopped, pretending to struggle to remove it.

37
00:03:24.878 --> 00:03:29.098
"Oof! The chain is tangled in my hair."

38
00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:31.207
"Let me help," Lainie said.

39
00:03:31.208 --> 00:03:34.547
But Ally was ready with her plan. "I've got it."

40
00:03:34.548 --> 00:03:38.507
She backed away toward the bathroom.

41
00:03:38.508 --> 00:03:41.685
"I just need to see what I'm doing in the mirror."

42
00:03:41.686 --> 00:03:46.415
Ally ducked into the bathroom and pulled her medallion off.

43
00:03:46.416 --> 00:03:48.999
Then she slipped it under the door.

44
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.494
"Here, you can look at it while I get the knots out of my hair."

45
00:03:52.495 --> 00:03:54.116
"Thanks!"

46
00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:58.791
Ally crouched to watch through the keyhole as Lainie examined the medallion.

47
00:03:58.792 --> 00:04:03.763
She turned it over, felt the weight in her hand; she even sniffed it.

48
00:04:03.764 --> 00:04:10.800
But just as she was about to slip it on over her head, the sounds of shouting erupted outside the pod.

49
00:04:10.801 --> 00:04:15.856
"Blast it! People have discovered my P.O.D.!" Lainie cried.

50
00:04:15.857 --> 00:04:23.622
She ran out of the P.O.D., Ally's meld medallion clutched in her hand!

51
00:04:23.623 --> 00:04:28.587
"Oh no!" Ally moaned, looking at herself in the mirror.

52
00:04:28.588 --> 00:04:33.770
"I can't let anyone see me looking like an Astralian! What do I do?

53
00:04:33.771 --> 00:04:40.506
I wish Mateo was here. If only I had a comm device. . . . Wait, I do!"

54
00:04:40.507 --> 00:04:46.957
Ally pulled Alpha out of her pocket. "Alpha," she commanded, "call Mateo."

55
00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:51.791
The phone rang once, twice, three times.

56
00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:56.880
"Come on, Mateo. Please answer this call!" Ally whispered.

57
00:04:56.881 --> 00:05:00.465
On the fourth ring, she finally heard Mateo's voice.

58
00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.112
"Hello?" he said.

59
00:05:02.113 --> 00:05:04.712
"Mateo! Quick! I need you to—"

60
00:05:04.713 --> 00:05:07.462
"This is Mateo," his voice continued.

61
00:05:07.463 --> 00:05:10.045
"I'm sorry I can't get to my phone right now.

62
00:05:10.046 --> 00:05:15.264
Please leave a message, and I'll get back to you as soon as I can." Beeep!

63
00:05:15.265 --> 00:05:18.365
Ally sank to the floor.

64
00:05:18.366 --> 00:05:24.894
"What do I do now? Without Mateo's help, I might never get my medallion back.

65
00:05:24.895 --> 00:05:30.712
This is awful . . . I'm doomed!"

